  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Georgia has received $6.8B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date, across 62,157 awards with an average award size of $109K. Obligations fell 41.8% year over year. The Department of Defense obligated $3.7B, the largest buying agency in the state, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services at $1.1B and the General Services Administration at $784M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest industry grouping by obligations at $937M, followed by Aircraft Manufacturing at $651M and Engineering Services at $581M. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP leads vendors with $579M, with MANHATTAN TORCON A JOINT VENTURE at $492M and GEORGIA TECH APPLIED RESEARCH CORP at $217M. FY21 through FY26 obligations show variation: FY21 totaled $11.1B, FY22 $8.5B, FY23 $11B, FY24 $10.4B, FY25 $11.6B, and FY26 $6.8B. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial, fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in Georgia changed this year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 41.8% year over year in FY2026 to date. Total obligations for FY2026 to date are $6.8B, down from $11.6B in FY25. Award volume remains sizable at 62,157 awards with an average award size of $109K. Fiscal-year series show prior totals of $11.1B in FY21, $8.5B in FY22, $11B in FY23, and $10.4B in FY24."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, industries, and vendors dominate federal spending in Georgia?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $3.7B, the largest buyer in FY2026 to date, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services at $1.1B and the General Services Administration at $784M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction accounted for $937M in obligations, Aircraft Manufacturing $651M, and Engineering Services $581M. LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP is the top vendor at $579M, with MANHATTAN TORCON A JOINT VENTURE at $492M and GEORGIA TECH APPLIED RESEARCH CORP at $217M."
      }
    ]
  },
